==Demographic==
[[Image:Haginochaya20051222 0950.jpg|thumb|150px|left|Dense Residential area in Shin-Kashiwaba]]
As for 2011, Shin-Kashiwaba has population of 468,330 people which is increasing from 442,590 in 2003. Though the peak population of Kashiwaba city was 700,488 people in 1956, Shin-Kashiwaba currently has it's largest population since the dismiss of Kashiwaba City in 1958.
Kashiwaba Metropolitan area which includes [[Kizawa, Maezaki|Kizawa]], [[Minamikashiwaba, Kinai|Minamikashiwaba]] and several neighboring cities has population of 1,420,580 people. The calculation not includes the neighboring independent city State Academy City since both area not considered to have any economic relation for their populations. If all 2,300,000 Academy City population counted in, the Kashiwaba-Academy City Metropolitan Area will have population 2.7 millions.

